        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "By default, SQLite does a checkpoint automatically when the WAL file reaches a threshold size of 1000 pages. (The SQLITE_DEFAULT_WAL_AUTOCHECKPOINT compile-time option can be used to specify a different default.) Applications using WAL do not have to do anything in order for these checkpoints to occur.",
        "title": "wal"
      },
      {
        "end": 375,
        "estimated_tokens": 45,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 14,
        "position": 1,
        "record_id": "ec3d4f55b0862ac30c2cb167",
        "score": 0.7213356678511696,
        "section": "wal",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 242,
        "text": "By default, the checkpoint will be run automatically by the same thread that does the COMMIT that pushes the WAL over its size limit.",
        "title": "wal"
      },
